# CS2 credentials

The CS2 server pod reads three secrets from a Secret named `cs2-credentials`
(see deployment.yaml). This Secret must exist in the `cs2` namespace **before**
ArgoCD syncs this app, otherwise the pod will sit in `CreateContainerConfigError`.

This Secret contains real credentials and MUST NOT be committed to git.
Create it out-of-band:

    kubectl create secret generic cs2-credentials \
      --namespace cs2 \
      --from-literal=SRCDS_TOKEN='<YOUR_STEAM_GSLT_TOKEN>' \
      --from-literal=CS2_PW='<YourPrivateServerPassword>' \
      --from-literal=CS2_RCONPW='<YourAdminRconPassword>'

Where:
  * SRCDS_TOKEN - Game Server Login Token (GSLT) for App ID 730, generated at
    https://steamcommunity.com/dev/managegameservers
  * CS2_PW      - Optional password players must enter to join (empty = open)
  * CS2_RCONPW  - RCON admin password

Reference manifest (for review only — do not commit):

    apiVersion: v1
    kind: Secret
    metadata:
      name: cs2-credentials
      namespace: cs2
    type: Opaque
    stringData:
      SRCDS_TOKEN: "YOUR_STEAM_GSLT_TOKEN_HERE"
      CS2_PW: "YourPrivateServerPassword"
      CS2_RCONPW: "YourAdminRconPassword"

This file is documentation only; ArgoCD ignores non-manifest files when syncing
the cs2/manifests directory.
